+::a5b1 I want to object to the framing rather than to the conclusion. ::a5b2 You have chosen three criteria that chocolate happens to satisfy and then declared a winner, which is not an argument, it is a scoreboard designed after the game. ::a5b3 If reliability were really the decisive property, we would all be eating industrial vanilla, because that is the flavour with the smallest variance of all.
